    "id": "train-287",
    "question": "Bran's tuition fee is $90. He does a part-time job that pays him $15 per month and he has a scholarship that takes care of 30% of his tuition fee. If he needs to pay his tuition fee within 3 months, how much does Bran still need to pay?",
    "gold": "18",
    "answer": "Bran's scholarship pays $90 x 0.30 = $<<90*0.30=27>>27 to his tuition fee.\nSo, the total amount he still needs to pay is $90 - $27 = $<<90-27=63>>63.\nAnd Bran will be able to earn $15 x 3 = $<<15*3=45>>45 after working for 3 months.\nTherefore, the total amount he still needs to pay is $63 - $45 = $<<63-45=18>>18.\n#### 18"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Bran still needs to pay for his tuition fee, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the amount of the scholarship.\n2. Determine the total amount Bran has already earned from his part-time job.\n3. Calculate the total amount Bran has already paid towards his tuition fee.\n4. Subtract the total amount paid from the total tuition fee to find out how much Bran still needs to pay.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail:\n\n1. The scholarship takes care of 30% of the tuition fee. The tuition fee is $90, so the scholarship amount is:\n   \\[\n   0.30 \\times 90 = 27\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the scholarship amount is $27.\n\n2. Bran earns $15 per month from his part-time job. Since he needs to pay his tuition fee within 3 months, the total amount he has earned from his part-time job is:\n   \\[\n   15 \\times 3 = 45\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the total amount Bran has earned from his part-time job is $45.\n\n3. The total amount Bran has already paid towards his tuition fee is the sum of the scholarship amount and the amount he has earned from his part-time job:\n   \\[\n   27 + 45 = 72\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the total amount Bran has already paid towards his tuition fee is $72.\n\n4. The total tuition fee is $90, so the amount Bran still needs to pay is:\n   \\[\n   90 - 72 = 18\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the amount Bran still needs to pay is $18.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
